# Git Co-Author Patch

## 🚫 NEVER
- NEVER append `Co-Authored-By` if the agent/environment already appends it natively (check git config or agent docs first).
- NEVER use uppercase in the email address. Email MUST be fully lowercase.
- NEVER use placeholder values like `<EMAIL>`, `email`, or fabricated addresses.
- NEVER omit the model identifier in parentheses when known.

## ✅ MUST DO
- If the agent does NOT natively append co-author, manually add this exact format at the end of the commit message body (after one blank line):
  ```text
  Co-Authored-By: <name> (<model>) <email>
  ```
- `<name>`: actual software name (e.g.,`DeepSeek Harness`, `OpenCode`, `CodeBuddy`).
- `<model>`: optional, include only when the model identifier is known (e.g., (deepseek-v4-flash)). Omit the parentheses entirely if unknown.
- `<email>`: use `no-reply@freewisdom.cn` by default.
- If name unconfigured and cannot be inferred, STOP and ask the user before committing.
- If <name> cannot be determined, STOP and ask the user before committing.
- Verify no duplicate `Co-Authored-By` trailer exists in the final message before executing `git commit`.
